          'Caustic soda is highly corrosive and can cause severe burns to skin and eyes. It is hygroscopic in solid form, absorbing moisture from the air, and reacts exothermically with water and acids. These properties dictate specific requirements for packaging, storage, transportation and personal protective equipment.',
